Let me implement with lightweight detection: find lines differing after normalization and report their keys.

```python
def block_field_diffs(a_text, b_text):
    def keyvals(s):
        out={}
        for line in s.split('\n'):
            mm=re.match(r'^  ([a-z_]+):\s*(.*)$', line)
            if mm: out[mm.group(1)]=re.sub(r'\s+',' ',mm.group(2)).strip()
        return out
    ka,kb=keyvals(a_text),keyvals(b_text)
    diffs={k:(ka.get(k),kb.get(k)) for k in set(ka)|set(kb) if ka.get(k)!=kb.get(k)}
    return diffs
```
